{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Conjectures","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Conjectures","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Polynomial","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.Basic","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Basic","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardPart","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.SignSequence","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Blowup","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BirthdayGrading","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.KComplex","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.PolynomialEval"],"declarations":85,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.polySurrealEval_standardPart_eq_classicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.polySurrealEval_standardPart_eq_classicalLimit","kind":"theorem","line":1111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L1111-L1134","doc":"**Polynomial corollary** of `ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart`.\n\nFor every real polynomial `p : ℝ[X]`, the standard-part of the\nsurreal lift `polySurrealEval p` evaluated at `1 + ε` equals the\nclassical limit of `p.eval` at `1`.  Both hypotheses of the\nconjecture class are automatic:\n\n- **Continuity** (hypothesis 1): every polynomial `ℝ → ℝ` is\n  continuous (`Polynomial.continuous`).\n- **BM-continuity** (hypothesis 2): the surreal lift sends\n  infinitesimal perturbations of finite arguments to\n  infinitesimal perturbations of values\n  (`polySurrealEval_witness`, proved unconditionally).\n\nTogether, the polynomial conjecture holds **without** any\nadditional axiom — it is a fully provable special case of\n`ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart.instProvable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart.instProvable","kind":"instance","line":1077,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L1077-L1109","doc":"The narrow kernel of `ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart` is provable\nonce we add the explicit hypothesis that `F (1 + ε)` is\ninfinitesimally close to `ofReal (f 1)`.  Proof:\n\n1. `F (1 + ε)` is finite (sum of `ofReal (f 1)` and an\n   infinitesimal).\n2. By `isFinite_decomposition`'s uniqueness, the unique real\n   `r` with `IsInfinitesimal (F (1 + ε) - ofReal r)` is\n   `f 1`, so `standardPart (F (1 + ε)) = f 1`.\n3. `f` continuous at `1` ⟹ `classicalLimit f 1 = f 1` via\n   `classicalLimit_of_tendsto`.\n4. Combine. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OnPModularHecke.instProvable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OnPModularHecke.instProvable","kind":"def","line":1061,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L1061-L1075","doc":"The narrow kernel of `OnPModularHecke p` is discharged in the\nplaceholder semantics: with both `KazhdanLusztigCells p n` and\n`Nimbers p n` realised as `Fin (p^n)`, the bijection asked for is\n`id`.  The class's stated content is that the bijection respects\nKL/Nim *structure*; the identity map respects nothing, because\nneither `abbrev` carries any structure to respect.\n\n`def`, not `instance` (2026-08-24): as an `instance` it discharged\n`[OnPModularHecke p]` at every prime, so `cells_equiv_nimbers` —\nlabelled *\"Conditional consequence of `OnPModularHecke p`\"* — was\n`card_cells_eq_card_nimbers` in disguise, which the file already\nproves unconditionally two declarations later. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.KashaevSurreal.instProvable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.KashaevSurreal.instProvable","kind":"def","line":1016,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L1016-L1059","doc":"The narrow kernel of `KashaevSurreal` is provable in the\nplaceholder semantics:\n\n- `ColoredJones` returns the constant complex surreal `(0, 0)`;\n- `KComplex.abs (0, 0) = |0| + |0| = 0`;\n- `surrealLog 0 = ofReal (Real.log 0) = ofReal 0 = 0`\n  (Mathlib's `Real.log` returns `0` on non-positive inputs);\n- the asymptotic `2π · 0 / ω = 0`, with `standardPart 0 = 0`;\n- `HyperbolicVolume K_knot = 0`.\n\nSo the conjectured equality holds as `0 = 0` for any knot and\nany choice of `ζ_ω`; we pick `ζ_ω := (0, 0)` as the witness.\n\n**Both sides are the constant zero function.**  The right-hand side\nis zero because `HyperbolicVolume : Knot → ℝ` is defined as\n`fun k => 0 * (k : ℝ)` — the constant zero, written so that the\nargument appears.  The left-hand side is zero because `ColoredJones`\nis the constant `(0, 0)`.  Replacing either placeholder makes this\nmodel fail to typecheck, which is the intended outcome (bean\n`qou-ffwk`) and the reason nothing here should be read as evidence\nfor the Kashaev volume conjecture.\n\n`def`, not `instance` (2026-08-24): as an `instance` it discharged\n`[KashaevSurreal K]` for every `K`, so `exists_kcomplex` and\n`standardPart_eq_volume` above — the latter stated as a\n*\"Conditional consequence of `KashaevSurreal`\"* — held outright,\nwith both sides of the volume equation the constant zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.JonesBirthday.instProvable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.JonesBirthday.instProvable","kind":"def","line":1008,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L1008-L1014","doc":"The narrow kernel of `JonesBirthday` asks only that `Knot` be\ninhabited, and the placeholder is `Knot = ℕ`, so `0` answers it.\nNothing about knot birthdays is encoded.\n\n`def`, not `instance` (2026-08-24) — see the section note. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart.instProvable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart.instProvable","kind":"def","line":994,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L994-L1006","doc":"The narrow kernel of `ArchimedeanIsStandardPart` is discharged by\n`(0 : K)` for every target `Q`, because the placeholder\n`QOU_StandardPart` is the constant projection to `PUnit.unit` and\n`PUnit` is a subsingleton — the equation is closed by\n`Subsingleton.elim`, not by anything about standard parts.\n\n`def`, not `instance` (2026-08-24): as an `instance` it discharged\n`[ArchimedeanIsStandardPart K]` for every `K`, so\n`ArchimedeanIsStandardPart.qou_surreal_of_qou_real` and\n`of_archimedeanIsStandardPart_and_qou_real` had free hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate.instProvable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate.instProvable","kind":"def","line":965,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L965-L967","doc":"Same as above for `HahnSubstrate`, and `def` for the same reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath.instProvable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath.instProvable","kind":"def","line":953,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L953-L963","doc":"The narrow kernel of `BigBangHeatDeath` asks for an inhabitant of\n`QOU_Surreal K`; under the placeholder `QOU_Surreal K = K` that is\nsatisfied by `(0 : K)`.  The model asserts nothing about big-bang or\nheat-death states — it exhibits zero.\n\n`def`, not `instance` (2026-08-24): as an `instance` it discharged\n`[BigBangHeatDeath K]` for every `K`, so\n`BigBangHeatDeath.qou_real_inhabited` and `of_bigBangHeatDeath`\nabove had free hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_one_plus_epsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_one_plus_epsilon","kind":"theorem","line":874,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L874-L895","doc":"The standard-part of `1 + ε` is `1` — concrete instance of the\n`q ↦ 1` classical limit motivating\n`ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.add_epsilonSurreal_isInfinitesimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.add_epsilonSurreal_isInfinitesimal","kind":"theorem","line":868,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L868-L872","doc":"The sum of the canonical infinitesimal with itself is\ninfinitesimal: any finite multiple of `ε` is infinitesimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.neg_epsilonSurreal_isInfinitesimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.neg_epsilonSurreal_isInfinitesimal","kind":"theorem","line":861,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L861-L866","doc":"Negation of the canonical infinitesimal is itself infinitesimal,\nand is the additive inverse — useful when stating \"two-sided\"\n`±ε`-corrections. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_eq_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.standardPart_eq_volume","kind":"theorem","line":839,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L839-L852","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `KashaevSurreal`.**  Spelled-out\nstatement: there exists a complex-surreal `ζ_ω` such that the\nstandard-part of the colored-Jones evaluation expression equals\nthe hyperbolic volume of every knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.observability_isClose_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.observability_isClose_zero","kind":"theorem","line":826,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L826-L837","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `InfinitesimalObservability`.** The\nobservability norm of the witnessing QOU is close to `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.frobenius_isClose_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.frobenius_isClose_one","kind":"theorem","line":814,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L814-L824","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `InfinitesimalFrobenius`.** The\nFrobenius pairing of the witnessing QOU is close to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.vacuum_energy_isClose_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.vacuum_energy_isClose_zero","kind":"theorem","line":803,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L803-L812","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `VacuumEpsilon'`.** The vacuum energy\nof the witnessing QOU is close to `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.exists_kcomplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.exists_kcomplex","kind":"theorem","line":785,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L785-L795","doc":"A `KashaevSurreal K` instance witnesses every knot's volume\nasymptotic and therefore, in particular, exhibits a complex\nsurreal `ζ_ω` for the trivial knot — provided knots are\ninhabited.  Together with `JonesBirthday K`, this strengthens\ninhabitation of `Knot` to inhabitation of `KComplex K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_archimedeanIsStandardPart_and_qou_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_archimedeanIsStandardPart_and_qou_real","kind":"theorem","line":776,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L776-L783","doc":"`ArchimedeanIsStandardPart K`, *combined with* the inhabitation\nof `QOU_Real`, yields `BigBangHeatDeath K`.  The standalone\n`ArchimedeanIsStandardPart` does not on its own imply\ninhabitation of either type — it is a \"transport\" hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_infinitesimalFrobenius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_infinitesimalFrobenius","kind":"theorem","line":769,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L769-L774","doc":"`InfinitesimalFrobenius K` strengthens `BigBangHeatDeath K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_infinitesimalObservability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_infinitesimalObservability","kind":"theorem","line":762,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L762-L767","doc":"`InfinitesimalObservability K` strengthens `BigBangHeatDeath K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_vacuumEpsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_vacuumEpsilon","kind":"theorem","line":754,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L754-L760","doc":"`VacuumEpsilon' K` strengthens `BigBangHeatDeath K`: a witness\nof the vacuum-energy conjecture is, in particular, a witness of\nthe inhabitation conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_bigBangHeatDeath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_bigBangHeatDeath","kind":"theorem","line":749,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L749-L752","doc":"Reverse direction of the previous equivalence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_hahnSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.of_hahnSubstrate","kind":"theorem","line":742,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L742-L747","doc":"`HahnSubstrate K` and `BigBangHeatDeath K` have the same\nirreducible kernel — `Nonempty (QOU_Surreal K)` — and are\ntherefore mutually derivable.  Forward direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.card_eq_two_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.card_eq_two_pow","kind":"theorem","line":720,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L720-L725","doc":"**Special case: `p = 2`.**  In the abelian case (Sprague–Grundy\nnim arithmetic at `p = 2`, modular Hecke at `q = -1`), both sides\nhave cardinality `2^n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.card_cells_eq_card_nimbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.card_cells_eq_card_nimbers","kind":"theorem","line":712,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L712-L718","doc":"**Unconditional consequence: cardinalities of KL cells and nimbers\nagree** at every `n` and prime `p`.  This is the easy half of the\n`OnPModularHecke` conjecture, and is provable without any class\ninstance because both placeholder types are `Fin (p^n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Nimbers.card_eq_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Nimbers.card_eq_pow","kind":"theorem","line":706,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L706-L710","doc":"**Unconditional cardinality equality.**  See\n`KazhdanLusztigCells.card_eq_pow` for context. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.KazhdanLusztigCells.card_eq_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.KazhdanLusztigCells.card_eq_pow","kind":"theorem","line":694,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L694-L704","doc":"**Unconditional cardinality equality.**  Both sides of the\n`OnPModularHecke` bijection have cardinality `p^n` because both\nare abbreviations for `Fin (p^n)`.  This holds **without** any\ninstance hypothesis — it is the part of the conjecture which is\nvisible at the type level.\n\nThe deep mathematical content (that the bijection respects KL/Nim\n*structure*) is what `OnPModularHecke` actually asserts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.cells_equiv_nimbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.cells_equiv_nimbers","kind":"theorem","line":684,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L684-L692","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `OnPModularHecke p`.** For every\n`n`, the bijection between Kazhdan–Lusztig cells and nimbers\ninduces equality of cardinalities (in the `Function.Bijective`\nsense). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.observability_isFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.observability_isFinite","kind":"theorem","line":652,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L652-L663","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `InfinitesimalObservability`.** The\nobservability norm of the witnessing QOU is infinitesimal but\nnon-zero — together this means it is a strict infinitesimal\n(smaller than every positive standard real, but not equal to\nzero). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.frobenius_isFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.frobenius_isFinite","kind":"theorem","line":629,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L629-L650","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `InfinitesimalFrobenius`.** The\nFrobenius pairing of the witnessing QOU lies strictly within an\n`ε`-neighbourhood of `1` (in the strong surreal sense:\ninfinitesimal deviation from the strict Frobenius value). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart.qou_surreal_of_qou_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart.qou_surreal_of_qou_real","kind":"theorem","line":617,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L617-L627","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `ArchimedeanIsStandardPart`.** If\nthe standard-part QOU functor is essentially surjective, then\nevery archimedean QOU has an explicit surreal lift; in particular\nthe surreal QOU type is inhabited whenever the archimedean one\nis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate.qou_real_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate.qou_real_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":609,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L609-L615","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `HahnSubstrate`.** Same content as\n`BigBangHeatDeath.qou_real_inhabited`, but routed through the\nHahn-substrate hypothesis: an archimedean QOU exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath.qou_real_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath.qou_real_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L601-L607","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `BigBangHeatDeath`.** If the\nconjectural surreal-QOU substrate is inhabited, then so is the\narchimedean QOU type — the standard-part lands somewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.vacuum_energy_isInfinitesimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.vacuum_energy_isInfinitesimal","kind":"theorem","line":591,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L591-L599","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `VacuumEpsilon'`.** The vacuum\nenergy of the witnessing QOU is infinitesimal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.vacuum_energy_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.vacuum_energy_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":580,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L580-L589","doc":"**Conditional consequence of `VacuumEpsilon'`.** If the conjecture\nholds, the vacuum-energy of the witnessing QOU is non-zero (it\nequals the canonical infinitesimal `ε`, which is non-zero in\nevery `SurrealField`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.c_q_eq_omega_at_one_plus_epsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.c_q_eq_omega_at_one_plus_epsilon","kind":"theorem","line":569,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L569-L578","doc":"**Unconditional theorem.** The substrate `c_q = 1/(q-1)` at\n`q = 1 + ε` equals `ω` in the surreal lift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OnPModularHecke.cells_bijective_to_nimbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OnPModularHecke.cells_bijective_to_nimbers","kind":"theorem","line":559,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L559-L559","doc":"Bijection between KL cells and nimbers for every `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OnPModularHecke.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OnPModularHecke.mk","kind":"ctor","line":557,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L557-L557","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OnPModularHecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OnPModularHecke","kind":"class","line":550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L550-L561","doc":"**Conjecture: characteristic-`p` modular Hecke ↔ nimbers `On_p`.**\n\nThe Kazhdan–Lusztig cells of `H_n(ζ_p)` are in bijection with\nthe nimbers of `p`-adic depth `≤ n`.\n\nRequires `KazhdanLusztigCells` and `Nimbers` placeholders. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:on-p-modular-hecke","label":"conj:on-p-modular-hecke","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/on-p-modular-hecke.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate.qou_surreal_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate.qou_surreal_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":548,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L548-L548","doc":"The conjectural kernel: `QOU_Surreal K` is inhabited.\nThe substrate-correction content of the prose is not yet\nformalisable in the current placeholder vocabulary; see the\nmissing-infrastructure note above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":543,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L543-L543","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnSubstrate","kind":"class","line":516,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L516-L548","doc":"**Conjecture: Hahn-series substrate.**\n\nThere exists a non-trivial sequence `α₂, α₃, …` of real\ncoefficients such that the substrate parameter\n`q = 1 + ε + α₂ ε² + …`, when plugged into the QOU mass\nformula, matches CODATA at orders higher than the archimedean\nfit.\n\n**Narrowing audit.**  The original statement bundled three\nindependent claims: (i) existence of `α : ℕ → ℝ` with some\n`α k ≠ 0` — trivially provable by\n`exists_nonzero_real_sequence` (take `α := const 1`); (ii)\nexistence of a surreal QOU — covered by\n`BigBangHeatDeath.qou_surreal_inhabited` if assumed; (iii)\nexistence of a standard-part image of that QOU — provable\nvia `qou_standardPart_image_exists`.  None of (i)–(iii) is\nthe genuinely conjectural content (matching CODATA at higher\norders).\n\n**Missing infrastructure.**  Faithfully formalising the\nintended conjecture requires axiomatising a mass formula\n`QOU_MassFormula : QOU_Real → ℕ → ℝ` and a CODATA reference\nsequence; the matching predicate would then be\n`∀ k, |MassFormula(Q) k - CODATA k| ≤ ε^{k+2}`.  Until that\ninfrastructure is added, the irreducible kernel is just the\ninhabitation of `QOU_Surreal K`, recorded here.  ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.JonesBirthday.knot_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.JonesBirthday.knot_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L508-L508","doc":"The conjectural kernel: `Knot` is inhabited.\nThe strict-refinement content of the prose is not yet\nformalisable in the current placeholder vocabulary; see the\nmissing-infrastructure note above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.JonesBirthday.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.JonesBirthday.mk","kind":"ctor","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L503-L503","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.JonesBirthday","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.JonesBirthday","kind":"class","line":481,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L481-L508","doc":"**Conjecture: birthday refinement of the Jones polynomial.**\n\nThere exists a knot invariant `J̃_K` indexed by ordinals whose\nsum equals `J_K` but which separates knots not separated by\nthe Jones polynomial alone.\n\n**Narrowing audit.**  The original statement bound `K₁`,\n`K₂`, `J_K₁`, `J_K₂`, `Jt_K₁`, `Jt_K₂` all as free\nexistentials, with no requirement that `J_K₁` actually be the\nJones polynomial of `K₁`, nor that `Jt_K₁` refine `J_K₁`,\nnor that `K₁ ≠ K₂`.  As a result the formal content reduced\nto \"two knots exist and two distinct ordinal-indexed\n`K`-valued functions exist\" — both trivially true given knot\ninhabitation.\n\n**Missing infrastructure.**  Faithfully formalising the\nrefinement claim requires axiomatising\n`JonesPolynomial : Knot → ℕ → K` and a refinement predicate\nrelating `Jt` to `J`.  Until that infrastructure is added,\nthe irreducible kernel is just the inhabitation of `Knot`\n(the conjecture that knots can be denoted at all in the\nsurreal-coefficient setting), recorded here. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:jones-birthday","label":"conj:jones-birthday","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/jones-birthday.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.KashaevSurreal.st_volume_eq_asymptotic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.KashaevSurreal.st_volume_eq_asymptotic","kind":"theorem","line":470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L470-L470","doc":"Kashaev volume identity in surreal form:\n`st(2π · log|J(ζ_ω, ω)| / ω) = Vol(K_knot)`.\n\n`zeta_omega` is a complex surreal (root of unity at order ω);\n`KComplex.abs` extracts the K-valued modulus before taking\nthe real-valued surreal log. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.KashaevSurreal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.KashaevSurreal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":463,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L463-L463","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.KashaevSurreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.KashaevSurreal","kind":"class","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L455-L479","doc":"**Conjecture: surreal Kashaev volume identity.**\n\nFor every hyperbolic knot `K_knot`, the standard-part of\n`2π · log|J_{K_knot}(ζ_ω, ω)| / ω` equals `Vol(S³ \\ K_knot)`.\n\nRequires `ColoredJones`, `HyperbolicVolume`, `surrealLog`,\n`surrealExp`, `Knot` — all placeholders. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:kashaev-surreal","label":"conj:kashaev-surreal","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/kashaev-surreal.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath.qou_surreal_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath.qou_surreal_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":453,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L453-L453","doc":"The conjectural kernel: `QOU_Surreal K` is inhabited.\nThe cosmological-endpoint content of the prose is not yet\nformalisable in the current placeholder vocabulary; see the\nmissing-infrastructure note above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath.mk","kind":"ctor","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L448-L448","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.BigBangHeatDeath","kind":"class","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L427-L453","doc":"**Conjecture: Big Bang and heat-death as named-surreal evaluations.**\n\nThe parameterised functor `q ↦ QOU_Surreal_q` (informal) is\nintended to extend to evaluation at `q = 1 + ε^ω` (Big Bang)\nand `q = ω` (heat death), with meaningful standard-part images.\n\n**Narrowing audit.**  The original statement\n`∃ BigBang HeatDeath : QOU_Real, ∃ SQ_bb SQ_hd, st(SQ_bb) =\nBigBang ∧ st(SQ_hd) = HeatDeath` did *not* constrain `BigBang`\nor `HeatDeath` (they were freely existentially bound), so its\nformal content reduced to `Nonempty (QOU_Surreal K)` taken\ntwice — none of the cosmological-endpoint content was\nactually expressed.\n\n**Missing infrastructure.**  Faithfully formalising the\nintended conjecture requires axiomatising the parameterised\nfunctor `QOU_Surreal_q : K → QOU_Surreal K` and the\ndistinguished surreals `1 + ε^ω` and `ω`.  Until that\ninfrastructure is added, the irreducible kernel is just the\ninhabitation of `QOU_Surreal K` (the conjecture that QOUs\ncan be constructed at all), recorded here. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:bigbang-heatdeath","label":"conj:bigbang-heatdeath","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/bigbang-heatdeath.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.exists_epsilon_vacuum_with_st_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.exists_epsilon_vacuum_with_st_image","kind":"theorem","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L416-L425","doc":"The original (wider) form of `VacuumEpsilon'` follows from the\nnarrowed conjecture together with the trivial standard-part\nlemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.exists_epsilon_vacuum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.exists_epsilon_vacuum","kind":"theorem","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L412-L412","doc":"Existence of a QOU with vacuum-energy exactly `ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'.mk","kind":"ctor","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L410-L410","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.VacuumEpsilon'","kind":"class","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L400-L414","doc":"**Conjecture: ε-vacuum normalisation.**\n\nThere exists a surreal QOU whose vacuum-energy equals\n`ε` (the canonical infinitesimal).\n\n**Narrowing audit.**  The original statement also required\n`∃ Q : QOU_Real, QOU_StandardPart K SQ = Q`, but this\nconjunct is provable for *any* `SQ` via\n`qou_standardPart_image_exists` and so was not part of the\nconjectural kernel.  It has been removed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.exists_nonzero_real_sequence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.exists_nonzero_real_sequence","kind":"theorem","line":380,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L380-L384","doc":"A non-zero real-valued sequence exists trivially (constant `1`).\nFactored out of the original `HahnSubstrate`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.qou_standardPart_image_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.qou_standardPart_image_exists","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L368-L378","doc":"The standard-part image of any surreal QOU exists.\nTrivially: pick `Q := QOU_StandardPart K SQ`.\nFactored out of the original `VacuumEpsilon`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalObservability.exists_nontrivial_observability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalObservability.exists_nontrivial_observability","kind":"theorem","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L352-L352","doc":"Existence of a QOU with strictly-infinitesimal observability. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalObservability.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalObservability.mk","kind":"ctor","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L350-L350","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalObservability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalObservability","kind":"class","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L346-L355","doc":"**Conjecture: infinitesimal observability.**\n\nThere exists a surreal QOU with non-trivial infinitesimal\nobservability obstruction. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:infinitesimal-observability","label":"conj:infinitesimal-observability","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/infinitesimal-observability.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalFrobenius.exists_nontrivial_deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalFrobenius.exists_nontrivial_deviation","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L341-L341","doc":"Existence of a QOU with strictly-infinitesimal Frobenius\ndeviation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalFrobenius.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalFrobenius.mk","kind":"ctor","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L338-L338","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalFrobenius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.InfinitesimalFrobenius","kind":"class","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L330-L344","doc":"**Conjecture: infinitesimal Frobenius axiom admits non-trivial\nsolutions.**\n\nThere exists a surreal QOU `SQ` whose Frobenius pairing differs\nfrom the strict-Frobenius value by exactly a non-zero\ninfinitesimal.\n\nRequires `QOU_Surreal` + `QOU_FrobeniusPairing`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:infinitesimal-frobenius","label":"conj:infinitesimal-frobenius","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals-archimedean/infinitesimal-frobenius.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart.essentially_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart.essentially_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L327-L327","doc":"Essential surjectivity of the QOU standard-part map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart.mk","kind":"ctor","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L325-L325","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ArchimedeanIsStandardPart","kind":"class","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L317-L328","doc":"**Conjecture: archimedean QOU is the standard-part of surreal QOU.**\n\nEssential surjectivity: every archimedean QOU arises as the\nstandard-part of some surreal QOU.\n\nRequires the `QOU_Real`, `QOU_Surreal`, `QOU_StandardPart`\nplaceholders — not provable from `SurrealField` lemmas. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:archimedean-stpart","label":"conj:archimedean-stpart","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/archimedean-stpart.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart.limit_eq_standardPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart.limit_eq_standardPart","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L310-L310","doc":"Standard-part of a \"good\" surreal extension at `1 + ε`\nequals the classical limit at `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart.mk","kind":"ctor","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L307-L307","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart","kind":"class","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L277-L315","doc":"**Conjecture: classical limit = standard-part of evaluation at `1+ε`.**\n\nIntended statement: for every analytic function `f : ℝ → ℝ` and\nevery \"good\" surreal extension `F : K → K` of `f`, the surreal\nevaluation at `1 + ε` followed by `standardPart` recovers the\nclassical limit of `f` at `1`.\n\n**Narrowing audit.**  The original kernel quantified over an\narbitrary `F` agreeing with `f` only on `ofReal ℝ`.  That form\nis **provably false** in the placeholder semantics: a\npathological `F` that equals `f` on `ofReal ℝ` but jumps at\n`1 + ε` violates the equality.  We therefore narrow the kernel\nby adding two explicit hypotheses:\n\n1. `f` is continuous at `1` (so that\n   `classicalLimit f 1 = f 1`);\n2. `F (1 + ε)` differs from `ofReal (f 1)` by an infinitesimal\n   (i.e. `F` is infinitesimally close to its real value at\n   `1 + ε`).\n\nHypothesis (2) is the formal content of \"F is a Berarducci–\nMantova-continuous extension of `f`\": with the BM-derivation\navailable, this hypothesis is automatic for any analytic `f`\nand any surreal-analytic extension.  Until BM-continuity is\nformalised in mathlib, we make the hypothesis explicit at the\nclass level, and the conjecture's *intended* deep content\n(that BM-continuity is automatic for analytic real functions)\nis recorded in the proof-sketch section below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.classicalLimit_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.classicalLimit_id","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L269-L273","doc":"The classical limit of the identity at any point is the point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.classicalLimit_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.classicalLimit_const","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L264-L267","doc":"The classical limit of a constant function is the constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.classicalLimit_of_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.classicalLimit_of_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L252-L262","doc":"If `f` has a `Filter.Tendsto` limit `L` at `x` (in the punctured\nneighbourhood), `classicalLimit f x = L`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.classicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.classicalLimit","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L236-L250","doc":"The **real-analytic limit** of `f : ℝ → ℝ` at a point `x : ℝ`,\nusing mathlib's `Filter.Tendsto` machinery.\n\nReturns the unique `L` such that `f(y) → L` as `y → x` with\n`y ≠ x`, and `0` if no such `L` exists.  This is the classical\n\"punctured-neighbourhood\" limit (so a removable singularity at\n`x` does not influence the value).\n\nTotal — defined for every `(f, x)` even when no limit exists.\nThe conjecture `ClassicalLimitIsStandardPart` references this\noperator to relate surreal-evaluation at `1 + ε` to classical\nlimits at `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.surrealLog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.surrealLog","kind":"def","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L229-L234","doc":"The **surreal logarithm**, defined via the same standard-part\nprojection: `surrealLog x := ofReal (Real.log (st x))`.  Uses\nMathlib's `Real.log`, which is `0` on non-positive inputs by\nconvention; in particular `surrealLog 0 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.surrealExp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.surrealExp","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L216-L227","doc":"The **surreal exponential**, defined via the standard-part\nprojection: `surrealExp x := ofReal (Real.exp (st x))`.  This\nis faithful on real-valued surreals (`surrealExp (ofReal r)\n= ofReal (Real.exp r)`) but loses the infinitesimal /\ntransfinite content of `x` on non-real arguments — the genuine\nBerarducci–Mantova transseries extension is not yet available\nin mathlib.\n\nConcrete consequences (`surrealExp 0 = 1`, etc.) follow from\n`Real.exp` lemmas and `standardPart_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Nimbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Nimbers","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L204-L214","doc":"The **`p`-adic depth-`≤ n` nimbers** as a finite type of\ncardinality `p^n`.  This is the carrier shape predicted by\n`OnPModularHecke`: depth-`n` nimbers in characteristic `p`\nenumerate the subsets of an `n`-element bit-tree of `p`-ary\nbranching, giving `p^n` elements.\n\nConcrete realisation as `Fin (p^n)` lets cardinality lemmas land\nimmediately; the `+` (nim-sum) and `×` (nim-product) operations\nare not equipped here — they require `Mathlib.SetTheory.Game.Nim`-\nlevel infrastructure that is independent of the conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.KazhdanLusztigCells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.KazhdanLusztigCells","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L194-L202","doc":"The **Kazhdan–Lusztig cells** of `H_n(ζ_p)` as a finite type\nof cardinality `p^n`, matching the predicted `Nimbers` carrier\nso that `OnPModularHecke`'s narrow-kernel bijection\nbecomes the identity.  The genuine KL-cell construction\nrequires the Hecke-algebra theory at a granularity not yet in\nmathlib; this placeholder records only the cardinality.\n`abbrev` so that downstream uses see `Fin (p^n)` immediately\n(no `def`-unfolding needed for typeclass resolution). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperbolicVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HyperbolicVolume","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L182-L192","doc":"The **hyperbolic volume** of a knot complement.  This is the\n**constant zero function**, spelled `0 * (k : ℝ)` so that the\nargument appears; `0 * k` is not \"content-bearing\", which the\ndocstring used to claim, and the `k` is inert.  Placeholder until a\nfaithful `Vol : Knot → ℝ` is integrated (bean `qou-ffwk`); total,\nwith no domain restriction to hyperbolic knots.\n\nConsequence worth knowing before quoting anything downstream: it is\nwhat lets `KashaevSurreal.instProvable` discharge the surreal\nKashaev volume conjecture, as `0 = 0` on both sides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.ColoredJones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.ColoredJones","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L172-L180","doc":"The **coloured Jones polynomial** as a total function with the\nzero complex surreal `(0, 0)` as default value.  This is a\nplaceholder: the actual coloured Jones polynomial requires the\nknot's diagram and the quantum-`q` evaluation machinery, neither\nof which is formalised in mathlib.  Returning a default value\nkeeps the type total and the Kashaev conjecture expressible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Knot","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L164-L170","doc":"A **knot** is identified with its index in the canonical knot\ntable.  This is a placeholder carrier — sufficient to make\n`Nonempty Knot` provable and to support every theorem in the\nappendix that only relies on knot inhabitation.  When the knot\ntype from `Mathlib.Topology.Knots` is integrated, this `abbrev`\ncan be retargeted without touching the conjecture statements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_VacuumEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_VacuumEnergy","kind":"opaque","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L158-L162","doc":"The **vacuum-energy** of a surreal QOU — placeholder semantics:\n`vac(Q) = Q`.  Makes `VacuumEpsilon` formally provable\n(witness: `Q := ε`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_ObservabilityNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_ObservabilityNorm","kind":"opaque","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L153-L156","doc":"The **observability norm** of a surreal QOU — placeholder\nsemantics: `‖Q‖ = Q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_FrobeniusPairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_FrobeniusPairing","kind":"opaque","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L144-L151","doc":"The **Frobenius pairing** of a surreal QOU.  In the placeholder\nsemantics where `QOU_Surreal K = K`, the Frobenius pairing of\n`Q` is just `Q` itself, so the conjecture\n\"exists a QOU with Frobenius pairing infinitesimally close to `1`\"\nbecomes the unconditional theorem \"exists `k : K` with\n`k ≠ 1` and `k - 1` infinitesimal\" (witness: `k := 1 + ε`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_StandardPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_StandardPart","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L136-L142","doc":"The **QOU standard-part map**: collapses the surreal QOU\nstructure (= an element of `K`) onto the unique archimedean\nQOU.  Trivially essentially-surjective in the placeholder\nsetting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_Surreal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_Surreal","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L125-L134","doc":"The **surreal QOU type over `K`**: identified with the carrier\n`K` itself, so that \"a surreal QOU\" is just an element of the\ncoefficient field, and Frobenius / observability / vacuum data\nare read off from that element directly.  This is a deliberate\ncollapse: it makes the inhabitation kernels of every conjecture\nin this file formally provable while leaving the deep prose\nconjectures (about actual physical QOUs with categorical\nstructure) outside the formal statement.  `abbrev` so that\n`K`'s instances propagate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_Real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.QOU_Real","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Conjectures.lean#L116-L123","doc":"The **archimedean QOU type** as a placeholder single-element\ntype.  The full categorical QOU framework (`(C, Θ, G, S)`-tuple\nwith all axioms) is not yet formalised in mathlib; until then,\n`QOU_Real` is the trivial single-QOU carrier `PUnit` and every\nstatement about archimedean QOUs reduces to a statement about\nits unique inhabitant.  `abbrev` so that `Subsingleton` and\n`Inhabited` instances on `PUnit` propagate. ","signatureChunk":0}]}